  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Building political support and enforcement capacity towards eliminating the trade in..Yellow-cheeked Crested Gibbons and other endangered species in South Vietnam</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This grant will build political will and institutional capacity for the successful implementation of enforcement campaigns aimed at eliminating the illegal trade in yellow-cheeked crested gibbons (Nomascus gabriellae) and other endangered species in Southern Vietnam. The Recipient will do this by: (a) increasing the capacity of the Ho Chi Minh City Forest Protection Department and Environmental Police in response, strategic enforcement operations and case investigations relating to the illegal wildlife trade; (b) improving methods and formalizing systems for the ongoing monitoring of illegal consumption of wildlife in retail establishments; (c) supporting the development of a local volunteer group Action for Wildlife Organization; and (d) building political will in the HCMC metropolitan area for wildlife crime enforcement operations, resulting prosecutions and placement of confiscated wildlife, through collaboration on a high-level political communication campaign.</narrative>
  </description>
